# GeoServer Configuration Demo

## Overview

This LiveBook demonstrates how to use the `geoserver_config` library to manage GeoServer
resources via the REST API: workspaces, datastores, coverage stores, coverages, styles,
and layer groups.

## Setup

Install the library and its dependencies. Adjust the path to point at your local checkout,
or replace with a hex/git reference once published.

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:req, "~> 0.5"},
  {:geoserver_config, path: Path.expand("../")}
])
```

## Connection

Build a connection once and pass it to every API call. The cell below reads from environment
variables. You can also use `GeoserverConfig.Connection.new/3` to supply values directly.

```elixir
# Set these in your shell before starting Livebook, or replace with literal strings here.
#
#   export GEOSERVER_BASE_URL="http://localhost:8080/geoserver/rest"
#   export GEOSERVER_USERNAME="admin"
#   export GEOSERVER_PASSWORD="geoserver"

conn = GeoserverConfig.Connection.from_env()
```

## Workspaces CRUD

```elixir
# GET — list all workspaces
GeoserverConfig.Workspaces.fetch_workspaces(conn)
```

```elixir
# POST — create a workspace
GeoserverConfig.Workspaces.create_workspace(conn, "my_workspace")
```

```elixir
# PUT — rename a workspace (may be rejected by GeoServer depending on version)
GeoserverConfig.Workspaces.update_workspace(conn, "my_workspace", "my_workspace_renamed")
```

```elixir
# DELETE — remove a workspace
GeoserverConfig.Workspaces.delete_workspace(conn, "my_workspace")
```

## Datastores CRUD

```elixir
# GET — list datastores in a workspace
GeoserverConfig.Datastores.list_datastores(conn, "my_workspace")
```

```elixir
# POST — create a PostGIS datastore
GeoserverConfig.Datastores.create_datastore(
  conn,
  "my_workspace",
  "my_postgis_store",
  "postgis",
  %{
    host: "localhost",
    port: 5432,
    database: "my_database",
    user: "db_user",
    passwd: "db_password"
  }
)
```

```elixir
# PUT — update a datastore
GeoserverConfig.Datastores.update_datastore(conn, "my_workspace", "my_postgis_store", "postgis", %{
  description: "Updated description",
  host: "localhost",
  port: 5432,
  database: "my_database",
  user: "db_user",
  passwd: "db_password"
})
```

```elixir
# DELETE — remove a datastore (true = also delete dependent feature types)
GeoserverConfig.Datastores.delete_datastore(conn, "my_workspace", "my_postgis_store", true)
```

## Coverage Store CRUD

```elixir
# GET — list coverage stores in a workspace
GeoserverConfig.Coveragestores.list_coveragestores(conn, "my_workspace")
```

```elixir
# POST — local GeoTIFF coverage store
GeoserverConfig.Coveragestores.create_coveragestore(
  conn,
  "my_workspace",
  "my_dem_store",
  "file:///data/rasters/my_dem.tif",
  "Digital elevation model"
)
```

```elixir
# POST — Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF (COG) coverage store served over HTTP
GeoserverConfig.Coveragestores.create_coveragestore(
  conn,
  "my_workspace",
  "my_cog_store",
  "cog://https://example.com/data/my_layer_cog.tif",
  "COG raster served over HTTP",
  %{
    metadata: %{
      "entry" => %{
        "@key" => "CogSettings.Key",
        "cogSettings" => %{
          "useCachingStream" => false,
          "rangeReaderSettings" => "HTTP"
        }
      }
    },
    disableOnConnFailure: false
  }
)
```

```elixir
# PUT — update a coverage store
GeoserverConfig.Coveragestores.update_coveragestore(
  conn,
  "my_workspace",
  "my_dem_store",
  %{
    type: "GeoTIFF",
    enabled: true,
    url: "file:///data/rasters/my_dem_updated.tif",
    description: "Updated description"
  }
)
```

```elixir
# DELETE — remove a coverage store
GeoserverConfig.Coveragestores.delete_coveragestore(conn, "my_workspace", "my_cog_store")
```

## Coverages (Raster Layers) CRUD

```elixir
# GET — list coverages in a coverage store
GeoserverConfig.Coverages.list_coverages(conn, "my_workspace", "my_dem_store")
```

```elixir
# POST — create a coverage layer
file_path = "file:///data/rasters/my_dem.tif"

GeoserverConfig.Coverages.create_coverage(
  conn,
  "my_workspace",
  "my_dem_store",
  "my_dem_layer",
  %{
    title: "My DEM Layer",
    description: "Digital elevation model coverage",
    abstract: "Raster coverage layer example",
    srs: "EPSG:4326",
    native_crs: "EPSG:4326",
    native_bbox: %{minx: -180.0, maxx: 180.0, miny: -90.0, maxy: 90.0},
    latlon_bbox: %{minx: -180.0, maxx: 180.0, miny: -90.0, maxy: 90.0},
    grid: %{
      dimension: [3600, 1800],
      transform: [0.1, 0.0, -180.0, 0.0, -0.1, 90.0]
    },
    metadata: %{
      "cacheAgeMax" => 3600,
      "cachingEnabled" => true
    }
  },
  file_path
)
```

```elixir
# DELETE — remove a coverage layer (true = also remove dependent resources)
GeoserverConfig.Coverages.delete_coverage(conn, "my_workspace", "my_dem_store", "my_dem_layer", true)
```

## Styles CRUD

```elixir
# GET — list all global styles
GeoserverConfig.Styles.list_styles(conn)
```

```elixir
# GET — list workspace-specific styles
GeoserverConfig.Styles.list_styles_workspace_specific(conn, "my_workspace")
```

```elixir
# POST — create a style (remove the workspace key for a global style)
sld_content = """
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<StyledLayerDescriptor version="1.0.0"
 xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/sld StyledLayerDescriptor.xsd"
 xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/sld"
 xmlns:ogc="http://www.opengis.net/ogc"
 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <NamedLayer>
    <Name>default_raster</Name>
    <UserStyle>
      <Title>Default Raster</Title>
      <Abstract>A sample style that draws a raster with 100% opacity</Abstract>
      <FeatureTypeStyle>
        <Rule>
          <RasterSymbolizer>
            <Opacity>1.0</Opacity>
          </RasterSymbolizer>
        </Rule>
      </FeatureTypeStyle>
    </UserStyle>
  </NamedLayer>
</StyledLayerDescriptor>
"""

GeoserverConfig.Styles.create_style(conn, %{
  name: "my_raster_style",
  sld_content: sld_content,
  filename: "my_raster_style.sld"
  # workspace: "my_workspace"  # uncomment to scope the style to a workspace
})
```

```elixir
# PUT — update a style
updated_sld = """
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<StyledLayerDescriptor version="1.0.0" xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/sld">
  <NamedLayer>
    <Name>my_roads</Name>
    <UserStyle>
      <Title>Roads Style</Title>
      <FeatureTypeStyle>
        <Rule>
          <LineSymbolizer>
            <Stroke>
              <CssParameter name="stroke">#0000FF</CssParameter>
              <CssParameter name="stroke-width">3</CssParameter>
            </Stroke>
          </LineSymbolizer>
        </Rule>
      </FeatureTypeStyle>
    </UserStyle>
  </NamedLayer>
</StyledLayerDescriptor>
"""

GeoserverConfig.Styles.update_style(conn, %{
  name: "my_raster_style",
  sld_content: updated_sld,
  filename: "my_raster_style.sld"
  # workspace: "my_workspace"
})
```

```elixir
# DELETE — remove a style
# recurse: true unassigns it from layers first; purge: true removes associated files
GeoserverConfig.Styles.delete_style(conn, "my_raster_style", nil, recurse: true)
```

## Assigning a Style to a Layer

```elixir
# Assign a style as the default for a layer.
# Pass the style's workspace as the last argument, or nil for a global style.
GeoserverConfig.assign_style_to_layer(
  conn,
  "my_workspace",
  "my_dem_layer",
  "my_raster_style",
  "my_workspace"
)
```

## Layer Groups CRUD

```elixir
# GET — list all layer groups
GeoserverConfig.LayerGroups.list_layer_groups(conn)
```

```elixir
# POST — create a layer group from XML
xml_body = """
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<layerGroup>
  <name>my_layer_group</name>
  <mode>SINGLE</mode>
  <title>My Layer Group</title>
  <abstractTxt>A group combining multiple layers</abstractTxt>
  <publishables>
    <published type="layer">
      <name>my_workspace:my_dem_layer</name>
    </published>
    <published type="layer">
      <name>my_workspace:my_vector_layer</name>
    </published>
  </publishables>
  <styles>
    <style>
      <name>my_workspace:my_raster_style</name>
    </style>
    <style>
      <name>my_workspace:my_vector_style</name>
    </style>
  </styles>
  <bounds>
    <minx>-180</minx>
    <maxx>180</maxx>
    <miny>-90</miny>
    <maxy>90</maxy>
    <crs>EPSG:4326</crs>
  </bounds>
</layerGroup>
"""

GeoserverConfig.LayerGroups.create_layer_group(conn, xml_body)
```

```elixir
# POST — create a layer group from a map (JSON)
json_body = %{
  "layerGroup" => %{
    "name" => "my_layer_group",
    "mode" => "SINGLE",
    "title" => "My Layer Group",
    "abstractTxt" => "A group combining multiple layers",
    "publishables" => %{
      "published" => [
        %{"@type" => "layer", "name" => "my_workspace:my_dem_layer"},
        %{"@type" => "layer", "name" => "my_workspace:my_vector_layer"}
      ]
    },
    "styles" => %{
      "style" => [
        %{"name" => "my_workspace:my_raster_style"},
        %{"name" => "my_workspace:my_vector_style"}
      ]
    },
    "bounds" => %{
      "minx" => -180, "maxx" => 180, "miny" => -90, "maxy" => 90,
      "crs" => "EPSG:4326"
    }
  }
}

GeoserverConfig.LayerGroups.create_layer_group(conn, json_body)
```

```elixir
# PUT — update a layer group
json_update_body = %{
  "layerGroup" => %{
    "name" => "my_layer_group",
    "title" => "My Updated Layer Group",
    "publishables" => %{
      "published" => [
        %{"@type" => "layer", "name" => "my_workspace:my_dem_layer"},
        %{"@type" => "layer", "name" => "my_workspace:my_vector_layer"},
        %{"@type" => "layer", "name" => "my_workspace:my_extra_layer"}
      ]
    },
    "styles" => %{
      "style" => [
        %{"name" => "my_workspace:my_raster_style"},
        %{"name" => "my_workspace:my_vector_style"},
        %{"name" => "my_workspace:my_extra_style"}
      ]
    }
  }
}

GeoserverConfig.LayerGroups.update_layer_group(conn, "my_layer_group", json_update_body)
```

```elixir
# Add a single layer to an existing group
GeoserverConfig.LayerGroups.add_layer_to_group(
  conn,
  "my_layer_group",
  "my_workspace:my_extra_layer",
  "my_workspace:my_extra_style"
)
```

```elixir
# Remove a single layer from a group
GeoserverConfig.LayerGroups.remove_layer_from_group(
  conn,
  "my_layer_group",
  "my_workspace:my_extra_layer"
)
```

```elixir
# DELETE — remove a layer group
GeoserverConfig.LayerGroups.delete_layer_group(conn, "my_layer_group")
```
